course: dictionary
lesson: 6569
title: An old word: nigh
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Nigh» is an old word that means near. You will meet it mostly in old stories, poems, fairy tales and the Bible, or in jokes. «The end is nigh» means the end is near, so it will come soon.
explain: Nigh can also mean almost. «It took nigh on an hour» means it took almost an hour. The word «hour» is your clue, and nigh on tells you the time was close to an hour.
explain: «Well nigh impossible» means almost impossible. Try the swap test: put «nearly» in place of «nigh». «Nearly impossible» still makes sense, so nigh must mean nearly here.
explain: Some people in parts of England still say nigh for near in everyday speech. «Draw nigh» means come closer, so when someone draws nigh, they are getting nearer.
fact: «Nigh» means near, either in place or in time.
fact: «Nigh on» means almost or nearly, as in «nigh on an hour».
fact: «Well nigh» also means almost, as in «well nigh impossible».
fact: «Nigh» can be an adjective, an adverb or a preposition, and the adjective changes to nigher and nighest.
fact: You will find «nigh» in old stories, poems and fairy tales, and some people in parts of England still use it for near.
exercise: «The end is nigh.» What does nigh mean here? | Under the water | Very loud | *Near, so it will come soon | Far away, so there is lots of time left
exercise: «It took nigh on an hour.» What does nigh on mean? | *Almost, or nearly | Never | Exactly, to the second | Less than a minute
exercise: «Well nigh impossible» means what? | *Almost impossible | Possible for certain | Nothing to do with it | Very easy to do
test: In «It took nigh on an hour», which word could replace nigh? | silly | *nearly | under | ago
test: In «Draw nigh», what does draw nigh mean? | Draw a picture | Go far away | *Come closer | Fall asleep
exam: Which sentence uses nigh to mean near in time, so something is coming soon? | We went nigh | Nigh a dog barked | The sun is nigh bright | *The end is nigh
